// Title: Launch Agent/Daemon Execution Via Launchctl
// Sigma ID: ae9d710f-dcd1-4f75-a0a5-93a73b5dda0e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Pratinav Chandra
// Date: 2024-05-13 | Modified: 2026-08-07
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, persistence, T1569.001, T1543.001, T1543.004
// Description: Detects the execution of programs as Launch Agents or Launch Daemons using launchctl on macOS.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities is expected to trigger false positives. Investigate the command line being passed to determine if the service or launch agent are suspicious.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1569.001/T1569.001.md
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/labs/20-common-tools-techniques-used-by-macos-threat-actors-malware/
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/2020/07/16/mac-cryptocurrency-trading-application-rebranded-bundled-malware/
//   - https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/18/d/new-macos-backdoor-linked-to-oceanlotus-found.html
//   - https://www.loobins.io/binaries/launchctl/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/725ea1eb2d7b42660c095f27cd83b1595378b068/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_launchctl_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/launchctl" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "submit" or ProcessCommandLine contains "load" or ProcessCommandLine contains "start" or ProcessCommandLine contains "bootstrap")
